{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1187310-how-do-you-roleplay-it-and-how-do-you-behave-as-a-true-faith-character","id":1187310,"title":"How do you roleplay it and how do you behave as a True faith character?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-18T10:21:42-08:00","id":1187310,"title":"How do you roleplay it and how do you behave as a True faith character?","content":"Now, I have a nack for making characters that seem to be from borderline epic and hard to do in practice.Well right now I'm trying out True faith as a way to exist as a human, how do I roleplay being a faithfull character, do I abide the holy rules of my religion or is there a more open aproach or a mad priest screaming &quot; INFIDEL &quot; and &quot; HERECY&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also, how does a Faithfull vampire act, does he hate his own existance, does he consider himself holy or destined to bring God's justice to the kindred society or does he just rip his own head off?<br /> Idea for the vampire is a 600 year old Vampire crusader who's given a divine warning about the start of the inquisition and he would go to sleep away the years and wake up at the end of 1990s to the new world that has changed and probablly be the one who has the job of re-booting the inqusition.On paper the plot sounds badass and a pretty good movie, but how does this happen and how does this work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23861-phantomdragenoid","name":"PhantomDragenoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T12:36:15-08:00","id":1187334,"title":"","content":"Its hard to say, as nearly every canon example of a character with True Faith, in my opinion, is presented as nearly the exact opposite of what True Faith is suppossed to be like. <br /> <br /> That is, forgiving rather than intolerant, seeking to help the world and save souls, not burn it down as long as they get one fiend. <br /> <br /> Anatole was partially an exception, as he had his Malkavian madness mixed in, but also an essence of a demon (sort of) all mixing up his interpritations of what his True Faith was guiding him to.<br /> <br /> I am also of the opinion that True Faith should almost always be a defensive ability rather than an attack, only used offensively in order to save others in extreme circumstances when most other means would fail.<br /> <br /> I am assuming you mean some form of Christian, so in my opinion, such a character would act like a steward of mortals, willing to suffer for others, but seeing it as more important to save souls than bodies, (only between the two). They would cling to tenets of the Bible, but focus more on the spirit than the letter of the law. <br /> <br /> They very well might hate themselves for being a vampire, but might not. After all, if they are a Vampire, but have True Faith, is that not proof that not all Vampires are automatically Damned, or that you have still a soul? They might see it as a burden given to them so that others do not have to suffer it, or a test to endure? <br /> <br /> They could be the more typical divine agent/fanatic/crusader type, but, in my opinion, as I said, this seems to go against nearly everything True Faith actually talks about. Instead, I would imagine that they would concider very hard each Cainite they destroy, seeing if there is a possibility they might be redeemed, because once they are destroyed, it is too late. Most can not be, but some can.<br /> <br /> My suggestion might be to have the character joinn the Inquisition, or at least work together until he realizes just how incompatible their beliefs and oractices are, at which point he doubtlessly becomes a target, but might win some individuals over to his side.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T16:53:40-08:00","id":1187385,"title":"","content":"Speaking of True Faith as presented mechanicaly in the rules, isn't it weird that Mages can have True Faith?<br /> <br /> I mean, Mages are able to perform Magick because they believe so overwhelmingly, so insanely strongly in X that they can warp reality to their will. For a charcter that has a religious paradigm like a member of the Celestial Chorus or a Dreamspeaker Shaman, isn't their ability to do Magick proof of their True Faith? Their belief is so strong that it can alter reality, how can you have belief stronger than that? So I feel like True Faith isn't a merit that mages should get, because religious mages already benifit from their faith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T00:19:28-08:00","id":1187478,"title":"","content":"It was discussed somewhere, and one of the big differences is that True Faith is more of an ability that is outside of the Mage. Unlike Magick, they have absolutely no control over what happens, if anything, from True Faith, which may actually be stronger than true Magick, (or may not be).<br /> <br /> For Mages, Magick is sort of like hacking reality, in a sense. Making small alterations within the context of overall rules, even if you are sometimes forced to use outdated and forgotten backdoor systems from much earlier operating systems, (old realities). True Faith's abilities on the other hand are more like things that can completely ignore those rules, maybe like a support specialist giving you a free credit to your account as a one time occurence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1721,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","user":"Beckett","date":". 02-19-2018, 03:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T01:10:53-08:00","id":1187490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1187310-how-do-you-roleplay-it-and-how-do-you-behave-as-a-true-faith-character?p=1187385#post1187385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of True Faith as presented mechanicaly in the rules, isn't it weird that Mages can have True Faith?<br /> <br /> I mean, Mages are able to perform Magick because they believe so overwhelmingly, so insanely strongly in X that they can warp reality to their will. For a charcter that has a religious paradigm like a member of the Celestial Chorus or a Dreamspeaker Shaman, isn't their ability to do Magick proof of their True Faith? Their belief is so strong that it can alter reality, how can you have belief stronger than that? So I feel like True Faith isn't a merit that mages should get, because religious mages already benifit from their faith.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is discussed in Detail in The Celestial Chorus book. I for one treat True Faith as &quot;Hedge Magic&quot; for the Celestial Chorus in my games and don't allow Double Dipping and this is a suggested option in the book(as is the standard &quot;they can double dip&quot; and &quot;no Celestial chorus aren't mages they jsut have true faith..&quot;).<br /> <br /> <br /> I think the DA secrets book has probably the best writeup and examples of how to rp a Vampire with True Faith though to brings things back around to the OP. It gives general requirments of the character and player and the sort of things that might cause loss or gain etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T11:37:39-08:00","id":1187607,"title":"","content":"What sort of clan would I likelly chose if I want to go with a True faith vampire, in my mind it comes down to maybe a Brujah or a Ventrue but i don't know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23861-phantomdragenoid","name":"PhantomDragenoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T14:10:07-08:00","id":1187642,"title":"","content":"Well, any sort of vampire could theoretically develop it if clan isn't that important to your concept. Lasombra were most closely associated with Western religion and religious organizations, Malkavians can fit the mad prophet in the wilderness stereotype, Nosferatu are good for hiding in catacombs and bell towers, etc.<br /> <br /> Gangrel, Tremere, Tzimisce, and Followers of Set are the four who seem inappropriate to me\u2014either irreligious, pagan individualists, or cultishly devoted to a god of darkness whose sphere of influence doesn't lend itself to the way True Faith operates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T16:40:25-08:00","id":1187682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1187310-how-do-you-roleplay-it-and-how-do-you-behave-as-a-true-faith-character?p=1187642#post1187642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, any sort of vampire could theoretically develop it if clan isn't that important to your concept. Lasombra were most closely associated with Western religion and religious organizations, Malkavians can fit the mad prophet in the wilderness stereotype, Nosferatu are good for hiding in catacombs and bell towers, etc.<br /> <br /> Gangrel, Tremere, Tzimisce, and Followers of Set are the four who seem inappropriate to me\u2014either irreligious, pagan individualists, or cultishly devoted to a god of darkness whose sphere of influence doesn't lend itself to the way True Faith operates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gangrel often embrace rather randomly, for the simple reason that the person in question is a survivor. That doesn't preclude someone of faith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T18:51:54-08:00","id":1187713,"title":"","content":"That's true, I guess clan culture may owe something to Viking traditions, but it really doesn't prevent individual members from being of any faith. And Gangrel may be the most diverse clan in terms of who they select for the embrace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T23:07:56-08:00","id":1188081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1187310-how-do-you-roleplay-it-and-how-do-you-behave-as-a-true-faith-character?p=1187642#post1187642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, any sort of vampire could theoretically develop it if clan isn't that important to your concept. Lasombra were most closely associated with Western religion and religious organizations, Malkavians can fit the mad prophet in the wilderness stereotype, Nosferatu are good for hiding in catacombs and bell towers, etc.<br /> <br /> Gangrel, Tremere, Tzimisce, and Followers of Set are the four who seem inappropriate to me\u2014either irreligious, pagan individualists, or cultishly devoted to a god of darkness whose sphere of influence doesn't lend itself to the way True Faith operates.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Follower of Set is used as the example vampire for True Faith in the Dark Ages secrets section. Basically you have to believe your god(or Ideology) is Good. The Follower of Set with True Faith(vs Akhu) is the Follower of Set who full out believes Set is the warrior against the Tyrant god. The Lord of Freedom, the protector of the downtrodden.<br /> <br /> The True Faith Settite Freaks the SHIT out of Setites, Especially Religiously Dogmatic!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T07:13:11-08:00","id":1188164,"title":"","content":"Well I've also wondered ammong the mentioned, can you actually go beyond the 5 rating and what could the abilities posssibly be, I know it's a 1 in a million odds to show but still, it's still something to think about, are we talking about divine powers to basicly do anything possible? Split the sea like Moses or just bring god's wrath upon anything that wants otherwise?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23861-phantomdragenoid","name":"PhantomDragenoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T13:13:48-08:00","id":1188275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PhantomDragenoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1187310-how-do-you-roleplay-it-and-how-do-you-behave-as-a-true-faith-character?p=1188164#post1188164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I've also wondered ammong the mentioned, can you actually go beyond the 5 rating and what could the abilities posssibly be, I know it's a 1 in a million odds to show but still, it's still something to think about, are we talking about divine powers to basicly do anything possible? Split the sea like Moses or just bring god's wrath upon anything that wants otherwise?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> True Faith can go beyond 5, No it can't do anything really impressive like that. Though it may let you shrug off all sorts of supernatural powers and force even the eldest of Vampires to run away and cry in the corner.. its much more personal like that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T15:59:26-08:00","id":1188323,"title":"","content":"Go down to faith rating 6-10. It looks like with Faith 10 you could survive being burned at the stake and perform miracles like turning a vampire back into a human.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/True_Faith\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/True_Faith</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T09:37:28-08:00","id":1189245,"title":"","content":"How does True faith affect wws? Since they are supernatural creatures like any other, but are they on the same level as vampires in terms of damnation?<br /> <br /> And how do I treat WWs compared to vampires?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23861,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23861-phantomdragenoid","user":"PhantomDragenoid","date":". 02-24-2018, 12:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23861-phantomdragenoid","name":"PhantomDragenoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T16:09:49-08:00","id":1189306,"title":"","content":"In a VTM<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />A campaign, there was a brujah monk with True Faith. He believed that if being a vampire is damnation, it is a damnation lesser than the sacrifice of Jesus, and any vampire with faith, will and humility can seek salvation. He prayed a lot, counseled many other kindred against revenge, anger or envy and developped no discipline at all since he refused to burn any unecessary blood. He was 100% against violence. Because he was seen as a holy man by many, he quickly became a favorite of the local prince and was even protected by a lasombra, a sinner who masqueraded as a monk and tried (and failed) to make him fall.<br /> <br /> His True Faith could manifest, but only when he was threatened and especially if he was protected other. That his own Faith could hurt him was only a trial toward salvation. At the end he reached Golconda and became human, but lived only for a day before his lasombra protector embraced him again.<br /> <br /> He's currently in a monastry somewhere trying to find Golconda again, and his Lasombra sire is curious to see if one of his clan can hope for salvation too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16128-kalendeer","name":"Kalendeer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T17:25:38-08:00","id":1189316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PhantomDragenoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1187310-how-do-you-roleplay-it-and-how-do-you-behave-as-a-true-faith-character?p=1189245#post1189245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does True faith affect wws? Since they are supernatural creatures like any other, but are they on the same level as vampires in terms of damnation?<br /> <br /> And how do I treat WWs compared to vampires?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You are some how under the impression that True Faith has anything to do with Theology. It does not. Damnation does not come into play at all except in the mind of the user of the power. For example a Kinfolk with True Faith: Gaia is not going to be able to or want to stop a Garou from doing their job. <br /> <br /> It is Entirely in the mind of the True Faith users. Nothing more, nothing less. That being said generally the effects of True Faith on Garou is inability shapeshift and calming of Rage vs turning and damaging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-08T02:01:28-07:00","id":1252465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1187310-how-do-you-roleplay-it-and-how-do-you-behave-as-a-true-faith-character?p=1187642#post1187642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, any sort of vampire could theoretically develop it if clan isn't that important to your concept. Lasombra were most closely associated with Western religion and religious organizations, Malkavians can fit the mad prophet in the wilderness stereotype, Nosferatu are good for hiding in catacombs and bell towers, etc.<br /> <br /> Gangrel, Tremere, Tzimisce, and Followers of Set are the four who seem inappropriate to me\u2014either irreligious, pagan individualists, or cultishly devoted to a god of darkness whose sphere of influence doesn't lend itself to the way True Faith operates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's not neglect dark faiths. Fanatical love of God, or an Antediluvian, or a being like Kupala. Or old pagan gods no one but the Vampire remembers. Tzimisce and Setites are viable for True Faith, it just might be the kind that makes the world a worse place. Then again not all Tzimisce and Setites are evil; a Setite could have true faith in Ra/Allah (a synthesis of Islam and Egyptian polytheism) and seek redemption. A Tzimisce embraced out of Grimaldi stock might have a fierce Christian faith.<br /> <br /> Someone with true faith 3 could be the best or worst person you've ever met. I like that it can be either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 09-08-2018, 05:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T21:41:05-07:00","id":1252942,"title":"","content":"I say a character that has True Faith has the spirit of the divine within him, and that should be roleplayed accordingly. Such a character likely follows their religious traditions faithfully and in a traditional manner, but those are merely trappings. What is important is how they live their life (do they love God or have the fear of God), and not the formal dogma of their religion. For people with low levels of True Faith, it is them being very devout and having a strong connection to the divine. They just need to be able to brandish a cross and be immune to some powers. For characters with higher levels of True Faith, study the stories of actual saints and how they are portrayed.<br /> <br /> I'd allow people with low True Faith to have negative qualities. If I run Dark Ages chronicles, a large percentage of the population has low levels of True Faith. It's one thing I use to distinguish that setting from modern day settings. So any number of &quot;Kill them all and let God sort them out&quot; might have it. Such people might have sincere belief, but it is out of fear of God, not love of Him. But such people won't progress in that True Faith. Higher levels of True Faith, (starting at least 6+, but perhaps even 4 or 5) need to be on the path of saints or mystics truly communing with the divine power and almost always represent the best instincts of humanity.<br /> <br /> I don't allow PCs (or NPCs) to have True Faith if they are supernatural characters (vampires, werewolves, etc.). Only ordinary humans, and I'd vet any PC carefully to make sure they are up to playing it properly (like I would any hard concept). But as much as I'd be interested in running an ordinary person/hunters chronicle in the WoD, I haven't had players interested in that.<br /> <br /> I also limit True Faith to the monothetistic religions, and any displays of power has to be appropriate within their religion. True Faith is all about the traditional vampire hunters of movies defeating vampires, and True Faith in the game should mirror that. The old pagan religions don't have anything like that - but I would allow them other Numina and Hedge Magic appropriate to them. I'd probably allow Buddhism to be more mirrored as True Faith than other things, but I'd have to study the folklore of Buddhist monks defeating demons and other monsters a lot in order to roleplay it properly, or be confidant the PC has done so to be able to do so as well (and of course, this varies widely within traditions, Theravada Buddhism has a lot less supernatural stories than Mahayana, but I'd probably still allow much of the &quot;power negation&quot; of supernatural powers that True Faith has). I don't know enough about Hinduism to know how best to roleplay that, but I think it would probably best be to use other Numina than True Faith to mirror the actual stories.<br /> <br /> I would never allow True Faith to be used for &quot;dark faiths&quot; or evil beings. Demons and stuff like that teach Dark Thaumaturgy or its equivalents to their disciples. They don't get True Faith for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T01:03:17-07:00","id":1253519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1187310-how-do-you-roleplay-it-and-how-do-you-behave-as-a-true-faith-character?p=1252465#post1252465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's not neglect dark faiths.</div> </div> </div> </div>V20 DA describes true faith as such<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For these people, faith is a raw but potent manifestation of will and positivity, focused through belief in a way specially attuned toward driving back the darkness. There are many ways for faith to manifest, such as healing, compassion, and group efforts to build civilizations or shake the heavens. When this manifestation comes, though, it is diamond-honed to respond to evil. It is, arguably, a natural human evolution in response to the ever-growing number of wicked monsters stalking the night. True Faith is a devout belief in right and beauty and light, and it burns brighter than fire. True Faith is a beautiful, empowering thing to witness, which is how it spreads. It is a burning, cold, powerful agony to be on the receiving end, like the single-minded burning of sunlight as it bakes the earth and blisters sin. True Faith (as it is often called by those Cainites who have witnessed it and survived) pushes back against darkness with light and very little regard for shades of grey. </div> </div> </div>So it needs to be Positive and focus on Driving back the darkness.<br /> It needs to be a force for Good","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T02:24:42-07:00","id":1253526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1187310-how-do-you-roleplay-it-and-how-do-you-behave-as-a-true-faith-character?p=1253519#post1253519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> V20 DA describes true faith as such<br /> <br /> <br /> So it needs to be Positive and focus on Driving back the darkness.<br /> It needs to be a force for Good</div> </div> </div> </div>V20 DA also explicitly talks about dark manifestations of True Faith; Tome of Secrets has a section on it. Here it's talking about the average manifestation you'd find in a knight of a holy order or a nun, which is relatively common in the DA and a huge threat to Vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}